  "adaptations": [
    "Native patch workspace and helper-v3 Agent/Verifier roles; existing Smith pipeline stays read-only.",
    "Preserve authentic naive package, frozen builder/search oracle and optimized GEMM reference patch.",
    "Public first four original workloads; hidden last two; final freshly measures all six, no added shapes.",
    "Hidden seed independently governs index construction and query draws; public seeds are the same in train and final.",
    "Preserve original two warmups/seven paired timed calls, median-of-ratios per workload and geometric mean.",
    "Independent log10 asymptotic score with S<=1 zero floor; no finite upper clipping.",
    "All-workload strict latency improvement and worst-recall non-regression against optimized reference.",
    "Original 0.99 per-timed-call naive recall gate; reject duplicate valid IDs and preserve -1/+inf padding.",
    "Float32 residual ADC consistency: rtol1e-6, atol0 after six-workload H100 calibration; zero oracle requires exact0 and legal padding is separate.",
    "Empty patch retains the original valid naive starter submission meaning.",
    "Stage/diff only package Python files including new/empty modules, exclude bytecode, reject every unsafe header/binary marker and unsupported rename/copy operation; candidate apply rejection preserves private final FAIL without inventing reference measurements.",
    "Replaceable store-final; formal answer18000 seconds and independent final5400 seconds; Verifier GPU16200 = train10800 + final5400, with short trials external only.",
    "Require explicit SIFT artifact checksum; missing data/configuration cannot produce a smoke score.",
    "Preserve metadata fields with truthful null/empty missing Smith history.",
    "Use one bounded Verifier GPU input upload without automatic retry; accepted failed or interrupted SSH execs consume quota. Preserve two-operation successful verification and existing train/final pools.",
    "Allow solver-authored local test_*.py modules under ivfpqlib consistently with the published new-Python-module contract; preserve reserved refivfpq.py/conftest.py, trusted outside paths and existing static safety checks. Official helper rejects reserved filenames explicitly without filtering payload files. No scientific measurements, scoring, workloads, reference, datasets or resource budgets change.",
    "Beat spec v3 (2026-10-08): add nn_recall (recall@k against exact nearest neighbours, worst of seven, >= reference) and two final-only hidden strict shapes (sift_q10k_np32, sift_q1k_np128_k1024); continuous score keeps the original six.",
    "Beat spec v3 release refresh (2026-10-11): reconciled with the local test-module contract; independent final limit 5400 -> 14400 s and Verifier GPU quota 16200 -> 25200 s ; statements updated; no workload, metric or scoring change. The new hidden shapes were measured once on one Modal H100 on 2026-10-11 (reference valid on both; see judge/beat_spec.json comments); not a platform reference qualification."
